    old "By the way, Wealthy-sama, you said you used to be a noble, but why are you a traveling actor now?{#ch5_6_v9976}"
    new "そういえばウェザリーさんって前は、\\n貴族だったって言ってましたけど、\\nどうして今は旅役者なんですか？"

    old "You know what, probing into a traveling actor's past is more than a little rude.{#ch5_6_v15875}"
    new "旅役者の過去を詮索しようなんて\\n野暮もいいところだよ。"

    old "I-I'm sorry.{#ch5_6_v9977}"
    new "ご、ごめんなさい。"

    old "Well, it's fine, though. By now, most of the mother country is already gone.{#ch5_6_v15876}"
    new "まあいいけどね。\\nもう、祖国はほとんど残っていないしね。"

    old "Gone...? Does a country fall that easily?{#ch5_6_v9978}"
    new "残っていないって……？\\nそんな簡単に国が滅ぶんですか？"

    old "You don't know what's going on in the world, do you. When a country falls, it's easy. Just like it's blown away.{#ch5_6_v15877}"
    new "きみは世間を知らないね。\\n滅ぶ時は簡単なものさ。\\n吹き飛ぶようにね。"

    old "…It's only when you lose your country that you learn its value.{#ch5_6_v15878}"
    new "……祖国というのは失ってはじめて\\nその価値を知るんだな。"

    old "Only when you consider the huge price of regaining it do people finally despair.{#ch5_6_v15879}"
    new "取り戻すための代価の大きさを考えて、\\nはじめて人は絶望するのさ。"

    old "At the place where I was born, I was taught that there are things more important than countries...{#ch5_6_v9979}"
    new "俺が生まれたところじゃ、\\n国とかよりもっと大切なものがあるって\\n教えられましたけど。"

    old "For example?{#ch5_6_v15880}"
    new "たとえば？"

    old "Let me see... equality... family... a lover...{#ch5_6_v9980}"
    new "ええと、平等とか、家族とか恋人とか……。"

    old "I wouldn't say it's wrong. But that's something only someone rich enough to be overflowing with wealth can say.{#ch5_6_v15881}"
    new "間違いとは言わない。\\nだが、それは富にあふれた人の言う台詞だな。"

    old "Wealthy-sama?{#ch5_6_v9981}"
    new "ウェザリーさん？"

    old "I think I talked too much. I'll go rest over there...{#ch5_6_v15882}"
    new "少し話しすぎたみたいだな。\\nわたしは奥で休んでることにしよう……。"
